    [BugFix][Attention] Fix Kimi A5 draft KV cache and FP8 MLA output (#18845)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fix the Kimi-K2.6 A5 wide-Eagle3 startup/stall issue and include the A5
    FP8 MLA output correction from #18914, so the FP8 main model and BF16
    draft fixes are available together.
    
    The existing wide-draft solution is preserved: concatenating two
    7168-wide inputs produces He=14336, which CANN MLA PROLOG_V3 rejects
    with error 561002. Eligible BF16 draft layers retain their original
    strided cache, write current rows through the existing RMSNorm/RoPE
    writer, and scatter into the original cache views. The bounded workspace
    is prepared during weight loading and reused for graph replay. Supported
    projection widths continue using PROLOG_V3.
    
    All four commits from #18914 through `9c1004335` are appended with their
    source commit references, including [zhaochuang001's latest
    helper-refactor
    review](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/18897#issuecomment-6207491634):
    
    - Request native `TND` for speculative A5 FP8 attention, preserving the
    raw FIA output buffer in captured attention parameters.
    - Route native token-major FP8 output through the existing fused V
    projection only for multiple tokens, no head padding, and `1 <=
    num_heads * kv_lora_rank < 65536`. Single-token FP8 decode, padded
    heads, and unsupported sizes retain the explicit head-major fallback.
    - Extract the common size predicate and FP8-only routing helper. DCP
    retains its original view, weight-dtype conversion, permutation
    arguments, single-token fusion, and BMM fallback. BF16 and A3 INT8
    decode behavior is preserved.
    - Include the CPU layout/shared-projection regressions, A5 eager/graph
    tests and projection benchmark, full Kimi FP8/BF16 Eagle3 generation
    test, and CI test registration.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Restores the affected wide-draft execution while retaining strided KV
    storage, and corrects FP8 MLA decode values for ordinary and speculative
    decoding. No API or configuration changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Independent before/after AST checks preserve all 55 existing
    unaffected MLA methods, including the wide-input adapter, cache writer,
    workspace, prolog, and forward routing. The original writer/replay E2E,
    cache-admission, DCP implementation, and related route/worker UT files
    remain byte-for-byte unchanged.
    - Each of the four appended commits has the same patch ID as its #18914
    source. The three new test files are byte-for-byte identical to #18914.
    - Local nine-file CPU suite using CI-pinned vLLM
    `c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b` with
    `VLLM_VERSION=0.31.0.dev0`: **952 passed, 233 subtests passed, 1
    skipped**. The skip is an existing worker V2 test. The suite includes
    the original wide-input regression and 116 FP8 layout cases plus 64
    shared-projection combinations.
    - A temporary clone replayed all five PR commits without conflicts onto
    latest main `b61c9b207f72e7765bf096a5dff2fc928a19b03f`; the same
    nine-file suite passed **974 tests and 233 subtests, with 1 existing
    skip**. Extra cases come from the newer main baseline; the actual PR
    branch keeps its original parent history.
    - Full `bash format.sh ci` and `git diff --check`: passed.
    - Mypy on the implementation and three imported
    layout/hardware/generation test modules with Python 3.10/3.11/3.12:
    passed. The modified `test_mla_v1.py` also has no diagnostics in the
    Python 3.10 before/after comparison.
    
    ```bash
    python -m pytest -q tests/ut/attention/test_mla_fp8_decode_layout.py tests/ut/attention/test_mla_v1.py tests/ut/attention/test_mla_prolog_v3_route.py tests/ut/ops/test_mla.py tests/ut/worker/test_model_runner_v1.py tests/ut/worker/test_model_runner_v2.py tests/ut/worker/test_attn_utils_v2.py tests/ut/attention/test_mla_pcp_dcp.py tests/ut/attention/test_mla_cp_workspace_owner.py
    ```
    
    Existing Kimi-K2.6 validation on #18897 was reported by the author; this
    update preserves that writer implementation. The newly combined branch
    has not been validated on A5 hardware. The imported suite contains 48
    eager/graph numerical cases and five projection benchmarks; the
    full-model test exercises TP4/DP2/EP8, FP8 main KV, BF16 Eagle3 KV, and
    repeated serial/concurrent requests against a no-draft baseline. Real
    NPU kernel/replay, combined full-model correctness, and
    performance/memory validation remain pending. CPU mocks and skipped
    hardware tests do not establish those results. CI is triggered by this
    push; completion is not claimed.
    
    
